From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philippe Simons <simons.philippe@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 22:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: encode at the frame rate set on the OUTPUT queue

The stateful encoder interface says VIDIOC_S_PARM on the OUTPUT queue
also sets the coded frame interval on the CAPTURE queue, and that a
client may then change the CAPTURE one if the two differ. iris keeps the
OUTPUT value in operating_rate only, while the firmware's rate control
is given frame_rate, which stays at DEFAULT_FPS for a client that sets
just OUTPUT. Such a client encoding 60 fps gets about twice the bitrate
it asked for.

Set frame_rate from the OUTPUT queue as well. A later VIDIOC_S_PARM on
CAPTURE still overrides it.
---
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_venc.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_venc.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_venc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_venc.c
@@ -414,10 +414,12 @@
 		goto reset_rate;
 	}
 
-	if (is_frame_rate)
+	if (is_frame_rate) {
 		inst->frame_rate = fps;
-	else
+	} else {
 		inst->operating_rate = fps;
+		inst->frame_rate = fps;
+	}
 
 	if ((s_parm->type == V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_OUTPUT_MPLANE && vb2_is_streaming(src_q)) ||
 	    (s_parm->type == V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_CAPTURE_MPLANE && vb2_is_streaming(dst_q))) {
@@ -433,10 +435,12 @@
 
 reset_rate:
 	if (ret) {
-		if (is_frame_rate)
+		if (is_frame_rate) {
 			inst->frame_rate = default_rate;
-		else
+		} else {
 			inst->operating_rate = default_rate;
+			inst->frame_rate = default_rate;
+		}
 	}
 
 	return ret;
